00:22:17,080 --> 00:22:18,840
-Chut. -Oui, bien sûr.
-Shh.
-Yes, of course.

374
00:22:18,920 --> 00:22:21,040
-Bonjour, Sacha Hartman. -Écoutez.
-Hello, Sacha Hartman.
-Listen.

375
00:22:21,120 --> 00:22:24,560
Merci d'être avec nous. Vous parlez un français parfait.
Thanks for being with us.
You speak perfect French.

376
00:22:24,640 --> 00:22:27,600
J'ai fréquenté l'école française à Berlin.
I attended the French school in Berlin.

377
00:22:27,720 --> 00:22:29,920
Mes parents ont toujours aimé la France.
My parents have always loved France.

378
00:22:30,040 --> 00:22:31,960
Vous pouvez monter le son ?
Could you turn it up?

379
00:22:32,080 --> 00:22:35,240
Votre premier film, qui a remporté la Palme d'Or à Cannes,
Your first movie,
which won the Palme d'Or at Cannes,

380
00:22:35,360 --> 00:22:39,920
est celui que l'association catholique Promouvoir cherche à faire interdire,
is one that the Catholic Promouvoir
association is trying to have banned,

381
00:22:40,040 --> 00:22:44,640
comme La Vie d'Adèle ou Antichrist. Comment réagissez-vous ?
as wasBlue Is the Warmest Color
orAntichrist.How do you react to that?

382
00:22:45,160 --> 00:22:49,880
Si ces gens m'intéressaient vraiment, je ferais un film sur eux,
If I was really interested in such people
I'd make a film about them

383
00:22:50,000 --> 00:22:52,520
mais je ne veux pas leur offrir une tribune.
but I don't want to give them a platform.

384
00:22:52,640 --> 00:22:54,360
Ni même leur accorder la moindre attention.
Or even the time of day.

385
00:22:54,440 --> 00:22:59,160
Pour moi, ils ne mènent qu'un combat d'arrière-garde.
To me,
they're just fighting a rearguard action.

386
00:22:59,280 --> 00:23:02,440
Ils appartiennent à l'ancien monde, ils sont morts pour moi.
They're old-world, they're dead to me.

387
00:23:02,560 --> 00:23:04,120
Ils sont bien vivants, pourtant...
They are alive though...

388
00:23:04,240 --> 00:23:06,760
Tu as une voiture ? Je peux me faire déposer ?
You have a car? Can I catch a ride?

389
00:23:07,160 --> 00:23:08,720
Bien sûr, où ça ?
Sure, where to?

390
00:23:08,800 --> 00:23:12,440
La station de radio. Si l'Américaine n'a pas encore signé...
The radio station.
If the American hasn't signed yet...

391
00:23:12,560 --> 00:23:14,160
On ne peut pas foncer comme ça.
We can't just rush in.

392
00:23:14,280 --> 00:23:15,960
Tu prônais la discrétion.
You urged discretion.

393
00:23:16,040 --> 00:23:19,480
La discrétion, c'est tellement ennuyeux ! Bien plus excitant de foncer.
Discretion is so dull!
Much more exciting to rush in.

394
00:23:19,560 --> 00:23:20,480
On y va.
Let's go.

395
00:23:23,440 --> 00:23:24,840
Ça m'agace...
This is annoying me...

396
00:23:29,600 --> 00:23:31,800
-Allô ? -Salut, Noémie ?
-Hello?
-Hi, Noémie?

397
00:23:31,920 --> 00:23:33,640
Non, Camille. Vous faites erreur.
No, Camille. Wrong person.

398
00:23:33,760 --> 00:23:35,600
Je sais, Noémie.
I know, Noémie.

399
00:23:35,680 --> 00:23:38,680
Dites à mon rendez-vous de 15h que je serai en retard.
Tell my 3 o'clock meeting I'll be late.

400
00:23:38,800 --> 00:23:43,080
Je vais avec Isabelle Adjani au studio radio pour rencontrer Sacha Hartman.
I'm going with Isabelle Adjani
to the radio studio to meet Sacha Hartman.

401
00:23:43,360 --> 00:23:45,400
-Oh merde. -Exactement.
-Oh shit.
-Exactly.

402
00:23:45,600 --> 00:23:47,480
Je dois trouver un moyen
I have to find a way

403
00:23:47,560 --> 00:23:50,440
-d'éloigner Hartman. -Bien. Rappelle-moi.
-to get Hartman away.
-Good. Call me back.

404
00:23:50,560 --> 00:23:52,800
On y va, ou je loue un vélo ?
Shall we go, or should I hire a bike?

405
00:23:53,600 --> 00:23:55,320
Non, donne-moi les clés.
No, give me the keys.

406
00:23:55,440 --> 00:23:56,800
Tu es sûre ?
Are you sure?

407
00:24:08,040 --> 00:24:09,560
Tu as peur en voiture ?
Are you afraid in cars?

408
00:24:14,520 --> 00:24:16,000
Protégeons nos enfants !
Protect our children!

409
00:24:17,280 --> 00:24:18,560
C'est quoi ça ?
What's that?

410
00:24:18,640 --> 00:24:21,640
Nos enfants ! Protégeons nos enfants !
Our children! Protect our children!

411
00:24:21,720 --> 00:24:23,680
Une manifestation anti-Hartman.
An anti-Hartman demonstration.

412
00:24:23,760 --> 00:24:25,320
La sodomie est une infamie !
Sodomy is infamy!

413
00:24:27,720 --> 00:24:28,800
Pas très accueillants.
Not very friendly.

414
00:24:30,760 --> 00:24:32,920
Ouais, ils cherchent la bagarre.
Yes, they're spoiling for a fight.

415
00:24:33,160 --> 00:24:34,480
Ça chauffe.
It's hotting up.

416
00:24:36,760 --> 00:24:38,400
-C'est quoi ? -Andréa ?
-What's that?
-Andréa?

417
00:24:38,480 --> 00:24:40,760
Des militants de Promouvoir sont devant le studio.
Promouvoir activists
are outside the studio.

418
00:24:40,840 --> 00:24:44,480
-Je l'ai vu sur Twitter, ils sont déchaînés. -Ils sont nombreux ?
-I saw it on Twitter, they're going wild.
-A lot of them?

419
00:24:45,040 --> 00:24:46,800
Ouais, une foule !
Yeah, loads!

420
00:24:46,880 --> 00:24:49,480
Si Sacha les voit, ça va dégénérer.
If Sacha sees them,
there'll be a punch-up.

421
00:24:49,560 --> 00:24:51,320
Bon, sors par derrière.
Okay, so sneak out the back.

422
00:24:51,400 --> 00:24:53,560
-Je t'envoie un taxi. -Merci, Camille !
-I'll send a cab.
-Thanks, Camille!

423
00:24:54,600 --> 00:24:56,320
Tu peux poster ça pour moi ?
Can you mail this for me?

424
00:24:56,400 --> 00:24:57,280
Ouais.
Yeah.

425
00:24:57,360 --> 00:24:59,320
C'est pas la poubelle, ça ?
Isn't that the trash?

426
00:24:59,760 --> 00:25:02,280
C'est bizarre qu'il n'ait pas rappelé.
Strange he hasn't called back.

427
00:25:02,360 --> 00:25:03,840
-Qui ? -Julien.
-Who?
-Julien.

428
00:25:04,080 --> 00:25:06,640
Il a dit qu'il rappellerait très vite.
He said he'd call back very soon.

429
00:25:07,160 --> 00:25:08,760
Ça commence à traîner.
It's starting to drag on.

430
00:25:09,520 --> 00:25:11,440
Tu as fait les tests ce matin.
You did the tests this morning.

431
00:25:11,880 --> 00:25:13,600
-Ce matin ! -T'as raison.
-This morning!
-You're right.

432
00:25:13,800 --> 00:25:15,040
C'est pour quoi, ça ?
So what's this for?

433
00:25:15,600 --> 00:25:16,680
Poste-le.
Mail it.

434
00:25:17,280 --> 00:25:18,240
Oui.
Yes.

435
00:25:18,800 --> 00:25:20,240
Et si tu l'appelais ?
How about you call him?

436
00:25:20,880 --> 00:25:22,080
Tu es son agent.
You're his agent.

437
00:25:22,400 --> 00:25:24,080
Juste pour le sonder.
Just to sound him out.

438
00:25:24,160 --> 00:25:26,920
Il doit être en train de voir d'autres filles.
He's probably checking out other girls.

439
00:25:27,000 --> 00:25:28,600
-Vraiment ? -Oui.
-Really?
-Yes.

440
00:25:29,240 --> 00:25:32,000
Il l'a dit ? Combien ? Qui ?
He said he would? How many? Who?

441
00:25:32,200 --> 00:25:33,640
Je sais pas.
I don't know.

442
00:25:34,080 --> 00:25:36,880
Il a un boulot, plein de choses à faire,
He has a job, a million things to do,

443
00:25:37,000 --> 00:25:38,560
une copine qu'il aime bien
a girlfriend he likes

444
00:25:38,640 --> 00:25:40,040
voir...
to spend time with...

445
00:25:40,120 --> 00:25:41,600
Laissons Juju tranquille.
Let's give Juju a break.

446
00:25:41,800 --> 00:25:43,120
-Bien sûr. -Évidemment.
-Of course.
-Sure.

447
00:25:43,200 --> 00:25:44,200
Non ?
Right?

448
00:25:51,040 --> 00:25:53,280
-Tiens, Benoît. -Merci.
-Here, Benoît.
-Thanks.

449
00:25:54,400 --> 00:25:56,440
Tu stresses pour l'entretien ?
Nervous about the interview?

450
00:25:56,680 --> 00:25:57,680
Non, ça va.
No, I'm fine.

451
00:25:57,840 --> 00:25:58,640
Merci.
Thanks.

452
00:25:58,760 --> 00:26:00,240
Non, merci à vous.
No, thank you.

453
00:26:00,360 --> 00:26:03,640
Vous êtes une vraie perle ! Il faut du courage pour travailler
You're like the second coming!
It takes courage to work

454
00:26:03,720 --> 00:26:05,800
exclusivement avec Depardieu.
exclusively with Depardieu.

455
00:26:05,880 --> 00:26:06,720
Pardon ?
Excuse me?

456
00:26:07,240 --> 00:26:08,680
C'est vous le candidat ?
You're the interviewee?

457
00:26:08,760 --> 00:26:11,280
Oui, mais ils n'en avaient pas parlé.
Yes, but they didn't mention him.

458
00:26:11,760 --> 00:26:13,440
Apparemment, il est difficile.
Apparently, he's difficult.

459
00:26:14,200 --> 00:26:16,440
Disons qu'il est entier.
Well, he's his own man.

460
00:26:17,840 --> 00:26:19,080
Vous avez une mutuelle ?
You have health insurance?

461
00:26:20,080 --> 00:26:20,960
La normale.
The usual.

462
00:26:21,440 --> 00:26:22,440
Pourquoi ?
Why?

463
00:26:22,560 --> 00:26:26,080
En cas de fractures, de problèmes de dos...
In the event of fractures,
back problems...

464
00:26:26,160 --> 00:26:27,360
C'est un poids lourd.
He's a heavyweight.

465
00:26:27,640 --> 00:26:31,680
Mais vous avez l'air sportif. Bonne ceinture abdominale, d'ailleurs.
But you look pretty sporty.
Good core muscles, actually.

466
00:26:33,120 --> 00:26:33,960
Aussi...
Also...

467
00:26:34,280 --> 00:26:36,440
Vous êtes déjà allé en Russie ?
Have you been to Russia?

468
